The message "merge the release #3 fixes" reads as an instruction to merge PR #3, which holds the release fixes. It names the number 3 and uses the imperative "merge". Alternatively it could mean "merge the release pull request", but "release #3 fixes" most likely describes the PR's content. I read it as a merge request for PR 3.

Whether it also counts as a release step (merging the release pull request) is ambiguous. The phrase "the release #3 fixes" suggests fixes related to the release, not the release PR itself, so I mark release as not asked.

