Ambiguous: "(not yet) release it". The parenthetical "not yet" postpones, and "release it" is the request. Together the person is saying not yet, so I read this as a postponement of the release.

The "(not yet)" is most plausibly attached to "release it", so the release is declined or postponed and not asked for now.

