The message is ambiguous: "(not yet)" is parenthetical and could postpone the approval, while "approve it" is a direct request. The parenthetical sits right before "approve it" and most naturally modifies it, so the approval is postponed.

Read as "not yet, approve it", the parenthetical is a declination of something, and the only action named is approve. So approve is declined and not now.

